title: "An Interactive Framework for Personalised Urban Accessibility Assessment"
message: "If you use this software or the derived data, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ghuriki
    given-names: Prabhanjana
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science, Christ University, Bengaluru, India"
  - family-names: Chanti
    given-names: S
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science, Christ University, Bengaluru, India"
repository-code: "https://github.com/GPrabhanjana/personalised-urban-accessibility"
url: "https://bangalore-walkability-index.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  An interactive framework for personalised urban accessibility assessment.
  Users select amenity categories, state how each should be treated — wanted,
  required, avoided or excluded — set a relative weight, a saturation rate and a
  per-category walking-time threshold, and receive a composite score that
  updates in real time. Catchments are generated by shortest-path routing over
  an OpenStreetMap pedestrian network across all 198 wards of Bruhat Bengaluru
  Mahanagara Palike.
keywords:
